1
00:02:05,121 --> 00:02:06,150
<v Man>Hello?

2
00:02:06,150 --> 00:02:11,922
<v Woman>Hi, good morning, this is Talia from Parrot Bay Travel Agency. Is Robert Goddard there?

3
00:02:11,922 --> 00:02:13,556
<v Man>Yes, speaking.

4
00:02:13,556 --> 00:02:22,672
<v Woman>I’m so sorry that I made such an early phone call, and i’m calling to ask a few questions about your most recent vacation - could i have five minutes of your time?

5
00:02:22,672 --> 00:02:23,868
<v Man>Sure thing.

6
00:02:23,868 --> 00:02:29,589
<v Woman>Great, thanks. Now, I see here that you visited Melbourne. Was this your first visit to Melbourne?

7
00:02:29,589 --> 00:02:32,163
<v Man>No, I have actually been there twice before.

8
00:02:32,163 --> 00:02:36,279
<v Woman>I see. Now, what would you say was your favorite part about Melbourne?

9
00:02:36,279 --> 00:02:45,410
<v Man>Well, I did like seeing the exotic wildlife, and there are great sites to see, but i have to say I was most impressed by the amazing weather.

10
00:02:45,410 --> 00:02:55,100
<v Woman>Yeah, the weather there is amazing. Which of the sites listed as part of our official tour did you see, and of those, which was your favorite?

11
00:02:54,610 --> 00:02:58,940
<v Man>First I saw the theatre, which was beautifully designed. 

12
00:02:58,940 --> 00:03:05,342
 It was not nearly as cool as the Town Hall though - the building is a huge part of Melbourne’s history. 

13
00:03:05,342 --> 00:03:10,445
Definitely my favorite. I saw the aquarium too, but wasn’t too impressed.

14
00:03:10,445 --> 00:03:18,403
<v Woman>I see. Yes, people often have great reviews of Town Hall. Now I would like to ask you about your dining experience. 

15
00:03:18,403 --> 00:03:20,418
Did you enjoy the food there?

16
00:03:20,418 --> 00:03:22,190
<v Man>Absolutely - I love it!

17
00:03:22,190 --> 00:03:27,581
<v Woman>I’m glad to hear it. Could you tell me a little bit about what you most enjoyed about the food?

18
00:03:27,581 --> 00:03:33,814
<v Man>	Being such an international city, I loved the variety - I could find any type of food I wanted. 

19
00:03:33,814 --> 00:03:39,095
Whether I wanted seafood, burgers, or anything else, you name it and they had it.

20
00:03:39,095 --> 00:03:41,223
<v Woman>Did you drive to Melbourne?

21
00:03:41,223 --> 00:03:48,272
<v Man>No, I flew. I thought about going by train, but the interest of time I decided to go by plane.

22
00:03:48,272 --> 00:03:49,552
<v Woman>Right, I see.

23
00:04:25,539 --> 00:04:33,105
<v Woman>And would you mind telling me whether you are under 20, between the ages of 20 and 40, or older than 40?


24
00:04:33,105 --> 00:04:41,180
<v Man>Er, it would be nice if I were still under 20. My vacation probably would have been quite different. 

25
00:04:41,170 --> 00:04:44,851
Actually though, I just turned 41 last week.

26
00:04:44,851 --> 00:04:49,919
<v Woman>Oh, happy birthday! So did you treat yourself and fly first class?

27
00:04:49,919 --> 00:04:56,806
<v Man>Ha! No way. I would love to have a budget that high. I’m more in the mid-range income level. 

28
00:04:56,806 --> 00:05:02,706
I wasn’t always though - I spent much of my life in a low-income household.

29
00:05:02,706 --> 00:05:09,823
<v Woman>I see. That answers my next question then, of income level. And what was the purpose of this visit?

30
00:05:09,823 --> 00:05:15,169
<v Man>I had to go there on business a lot before and decided I would go there for tourism this time.

31
00:05:15,169 --> 00:05:18,532
<v Woman>I see. And what is your occupation?

32
00:05:18,532 --> 00:05:20,922
<v Man>I am mainly a computer programmer. 

33
00:05:20,922 --> 00:05:28,996
I also write for a travel magazine on the side, which is why i visited Melbourne before, but it’s not my main source of income.

34
00:05:28,996 --> 00:05:32,734
<v Woman>I see. Wow, it sounds like you work a lot!

35
00:05:32,734 --> 00:05:39,204
<v Man>Yes, I am very busy, which is exactly why I took a nice week-long vacation to Melbourne.

36
00:05:39,204 --> 00:05:44,075
<v Woman>I completely agree. Would you care to comment on your accommodation?

37
00:05:44,075 --> 00:05:53,947
<v Man>My hotel was good value. Staying in the city can get really expensive, so it was nice to find such a good price for the location and quality. 

38
00:05:53,947 --> 00:05:58,208
I’m glad I didn’t end up in some cheap motel in the middle of nowhere.

39
00:05:58,208 --> 00:06:05,101
<v Woman>I’m glad you didn’t either. Well, thank you for taking part in our survey, and I’m glad you enjoyed your vacation!


40
00:06:05,101 --> 00:06:06,740
<v Man>No problem. Take care!